  "notes": [
   "Price sheet: 'Energy Produced credits are only applicable to Solar Billing Plan customers who receive bundled generation service from PG&E. Customers who receive generation service from a Community Choice Aggregator (CCA) ... should refer to their provider'. So 'Produced' = generation component and 'Delivered' = delivery component.",
   "Price sheet footnote 1: 'Pricing reflects the average EEC values determined by the California Public Utilities Commission. Hours and values have also been adjusted to account for daylight savings time when appropriate.' Hours are local clock time.",
   "Schedule NBT Sheet 11: export rates are built from the CPUC Avoided Cost Calculator; generation = Energy, Generation Capacity, Cap and Trade, Ancillary Services, Losses; delivery = Distribution Capacity, Transmission Capacity, GHG Adder, GHG Rebalancing, Methane Leakage; averaged by month, weekday/weekend and hour, with a $0/kWh floor.",
   "Schedule NBT Sheet 10: customers who apply from April 15, 2023 through December 31, 2027 get a 'locked-in' nine-year schedule of hourly values from the ACC adopted as of January 1 of their application year. This file holds the 2026 values only; Griddy holds them flat across later years (assumption).",
   "Schedule NBT: residential NBT customers take service on E-ELEC; CARE/FERA discounts are not applied to export compensation.",
   "PG&E+SVCE customers: PG&E pays the delivery component; SVCE pays the generation part under its own NEM-SVCE schedule ('credited for the electricity they export based on its value to the grid ... determined through a public proceeding managed by the CPUC', svcleanenergy.org/solar-billing-plan). UNCONFIRMED that SVCE's generation credit equals PG&E's 'Produced' values; Griddy assumes it does. SVCE also states a $0.017/kWh GreenPrime adder 'in the monthly credit rollover'.",
   "Annual net surplus compensation (cash-out) is not modelled; credits only offset charges within the year (assumption)."
